 "shape_hint": "A thin sheet-metal ring with one tab on the inside of the bore (width f1; it sits in the shaft keyway, M is measured from the tab tip across the bore) and a ring of narrow tabs (width f) all round the outside, set at about 25 degrees to the flat face; one outer tab is bent into a slot of the lock nut.",
 "role_map": {
  "row label": "MB<n> designation (pairs with lock nut KM<n>)",
  "d3": "bore diameter",
  "d5": "outside diameter over the outer tabs",
  "d4": "root circle diameter of the outer tabs = diameter of the flat side face",
  "f1": "width of the inner tab",
  "M": "distance from the tip of the inner tab to the opposite side of the bore",
  "f": "width of an outer tab",
  "B7": "sheet thickness (printed as minimum by some pages)"
 },
 "notes": "Candidate 38 sizes x 8 columns (7 numeric + nut text) -> kept 37 x 7. Column keys are the ISO 2982-2 letters used by the catalog; the pages use other letters, mapped through each page's own drawing or wording: DIN pages d1/d2/d3/e/f/b1/s, globalfastener d/dc/d1/n1/s1/n/h, SKF d/d2/d1/f/M/B, usarollerchain D1/D5/D4/E/K/S/T. Clusters: globalfastener (DIN 5406-2011 page; its 1993 page has identical numbers), fasteners.eu (+ boltport; MB0-MB30; their letter f is not explained by a drawing and is not counted for M), schrauben-lexikon (MB0-MB30), fasten.it (04/2011 table; prints no MB code, so its rows are matched through bore + outside diameter and it is never counted for d3 / d5), SKF product pages (rendered with a browser; no outer tab width) and USA Roller Chain product pages (some values rounded: T 1.2 for 1.25, 1.8 for 1.75, D4 13 for 13.5). MB31-MB40 rest on globalfastener + SKF + usarollerchain for d3 / d5 and globalfastener + fasten.it + usarollerchain for f (exactly 3). DISSENT TO DECIDE: inner tab width f1 at MB19 / MB23 / MB27 is 10 / 12 / 14 on five clusters, but the fasten.it \"04/2011\" table prints 12 / 14 / 16. fasten.it's own \"1993\" table on the same page prints 12 / 12 / 14 there and 8 / 10 at MB10 / MB15 (where its 2011 table and everyone else print 6 / 8), so that page disagrees with itself; globalfastener shows no difference between its 1993 and 2011 pages. If the fasten.it 2011 table were a true edition change, the three kept f1 cells would be older-edition values - not decidable without the standard. Single-page typos seen: fasteners.eu MB7 s 12,5; schrauben-lexikon MB12 d2 864, MB4 s 1,25, MB7 e 5 / b1 6. B7 is printed as a minimum by fasten.it (\"s min.\") and as \"Thickness material\" by SKF. d4 is the root circle of the outer tabs = SKF \"Side face diameter\". ISO 2982-2 and KS B 2004 texts were not compared.",
 "scope": "MB0~MB40 (MB8·MB19·MB23·MB27·MB29와 MBL 계열 제외)",
