 "verification": {
  "verdict": "partial",
  "cell_support_min": 3,
  "checks_done": "Independent re-fetch on 2026-11-11 with curl (browser UA, 2.5 s pause per site) of every counted and rival page; SKF pages rendered with playwright; drawings downloaded and read to confirm letter mappings. Own parser (html.parser with rowspan/colspan expansion) and own per-site extraction in scratchpad t2/g4v/code (v_mbw.py, v_sens.py); researcher raw/ and scripts not used. Counted only maker/distributor HTML tables whose header or drawing states the column meaning; 33 rows x 7 cols kept, every kept cell has >= 3 independent clusters with exactly the same number. Sanity checks recomputed on kept rows.",
  "problems": [
   "MB31-MB40: d3 and d5 rest on exactly GF + SKF + URC, f on exactly GF + FI + URC (zero slack; without usarollerchain these 7 rows fail).",
   "fasten.it matching: (bore, outside diameter) pairs are unique on both fasten.it tables and on globalfastener (51 MB/MBL codes); every fasten.it 2011 row maps to one globalfastener code and agrees on d4, M, f, B7 for all of them; only f1 differs (MB19/23/27). fasten.it is never counted for d3 or d5. Safe.",
   "Single-page rivals left in kept rows (not counted for those cells): usarollerchain rounds thickness (1.2 for 1.25, 1.8 for 1.75) and MB0 d4 13 (13.5); schrauben-lexikon MB4 s 1.25, MB7 e 5 / b1 6, MB12 d2 864; fasteners.eu MB7 s 12,5; fasten.it 1993 table f1 8 / 10 at MB10 / MB15 (older edition, one page).",
   "B7 is \"s min.\" on fasten.it and plain thickness elsewhere; B7 still has >=3 clusters without fasten.it.",
   "fasten.it norm sheets end with 'Reproduced by permission of DIN'. Counted (as in the earlier verified records kmnut/clevis/spring-co) because it is a licensed dimension sheet, not the standard's text, but EVERY family here falls to 2 clusters on many cells without it - if the lead rules such licensed reproductions out, all four records fail."
  ],
